Sometimes I'm learning lines.
有时我在背台词。

1032
00:57:10.750 --> 00:57:12.550
It's depending if I'm working or not.
这取决于我是否在工作。

1033
00:57:13.810 --> 00:57:15.290
What else do I like to do?
我还喜欢做什么呢？

1034
00:57:15.290 --> 00:57:16.490
I like to color.
我喜欢涂色。

1035
00:57:16.850 --> 00:57:19.390
I like to color coloring books and stuff.
我喜欢给涂色书之类的东西上色。

1036
00:57:19.390 --> 00:57:26.230
And I have, in fact, Jenny Ehrman, who wrote our series, just sent me a box of wonderful
事实上，我们剧集的编剧珍妮·厄尔曼刚寄给我一盒很棒的

1037
00:57:26.230 --> 00:57:29.710
pencils and coloring books because she loves to do that.
铅笔和涂色书，因为她也喜欢做这个。

1038
00:57:30.110 --> 00:57:33.230
And I have an app on my iPad that I love to do.
我iPad上也有一个我很喜欢的涂色应用。

1039
00:57:33.310 --> 00:57:34.030
I love to color.
我真的很喜欢涂色。

1040
00:57:34.390 --> 00:57:36.870
I love to listen to books on tape.
我喜欢听有声书。

1041
00:57:37.370 --> 00:57:41.750
That's one of the things I'm really starting to enjoy on my hiatus is that I'm now back
这是我休假期间开始真正享受的事情之一，我现在又

1042
00:57:41.750 --> 00:57:44.510
to listening to books and reading a lot of different kinds of books.
开始听书并阅读各种各样的书籍了。

1043
00:57:44.530 --> 00:57:48.730
I just finished a book called The Conclave last night, which is brilliant.
我昨晚刚读完一本叫《教宗选举》的书，非常精彩。

1044
00:57:48.730 --> 00:57:50.430
I know there's a film out about it.
我知道现在有一部关于它的电影上映了。

1045
00:57:50.490 --> 00:57:51.470
I want to go and see that.
我想去看看。

1046
00:57:51.930 --> 00:57:54.390
So, yes, I like to read.
所以，是的，我喜欢阅读。

1047
00:57:54.390 --> 00:57:55.690
I like to color.
我喜欢涂色。

1048
00:57:56.010 --> 00:58:02.250
I guess it's kind of like a, I don't know, maybe I'm stuck at 13 years old.
我想这就像是，我不知道，也许我心理年龄还停留在13岁吧。

1049
00:58:02.370 --> 00:58:02.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1050
00:58:03.310 --> 00:58:08.270
But those are the kinds of things I like to do and be with my dog, my puppy, and just
但这些就是我喜欢做的事，还有和我的狗，我的小狗待在一起，就这样。

1051
00:58:08.270 --> 00:58:09.250
very low key.
非常低调。

1052
00:58:09.650 --> 00:58:10.990
That sounds lovely.
听起来真不错。

1053
00:58:11.430 --> 00:58:16.750
Well, Kathy, you are such an icon of the entertainment business.
凯西，你是演艺界的偶像级人物。

1054
00:58:16.750 --> 00:58:18.050
You're such an icon.
你真是个偶像。

1055
00:58:18.150 --> 00:58:25.030
And I wondered if we could end the interview by asking you, what is the best piece of advice
我想在采访结束时问你一个问题，你职业生涯中收到过最好的建议是什么？

1056
00:58:25.030 --> 00:58:26.670
you received in your career?
你对有抱负的演员又有什么建议呢？

1057
00:58:26.870 --> 00:58:30.090
And what advice might you give an aspiring actor?
你对有抱负的演员又有什么建议呢？

1058
00:58:31.090 --> 00:58:36.650
Well, it all boils down to, someone once told me, you have to have a head like a bullet and
嗯，归根结底，曾经有人告诉我，你必须拥有像子弹一样坚硬的头脑，

1059
00:58:36.650 --> 00:58:37.630
a heart like a baby.
和像婴儿一样柔软的心。

1060
00:58:38.570 --> 00:58:45.790
And I could expand on that by saying, especially nowadays, with social media being so powerful
我可以补充一点，尤其是在当今社交媒体影响力如此巨大，

1061
00:58:45.790 --> 00:58:51.250
and powerful in negative ways, is that you really have to be, you have to get strong.
且负面影响也如此强大的情况下，你真的必须变得强大。

1062
00:58:51.810 --> 00:58:59.130
You have to get tough and at the same time, not get cynical or bitter, but you've got to
你必须变得坚强，同时又不能变得愤世嫉俗或满腹牢骚，你必须

1063
00:58:59.130 --> 00:58:59.930
protect yourself.
保护好自己。

1064
00:59:00.270 --> 00:59:06.630
I don't advocate being on social media unless, in your case, it's a great thing for your
我不提倡使用社交媒体，除非像你这种情况，这对你的

1065
00:59:06.630 --> 00:59:06.990
show.
节目很有帮助。

1066
00:59:07.170 --> 00:59:07.990
You need to do that.
你需要那样做。

1067
00:59:08.370 --> 00:59:11.930
But I don't want to read negative things about myself.
但我不想读到关于我自己的负面评价。

1068
00:59:11.930 --> 00:59:18.370
I just think that the best kind of advice I could give is, if you're serious about being
我只是觉得我能给出的最好的建议是，如果你是认真想成为

1069
00:59:18.370 --> 00:59:23.630
an actor, if you want to be an actor like Cillian Murphy or Anthony Hopkins or Cate
一名演员，如果你想成为像基里安·墨菲、安东尼·霍普金斯或凯特·

1070
00:59:23.630 --> 00:59:26.110
Blanchett, you have to study.
布兰切特那样的演员，你就必须学习。

1071
00:59:26.350 --> 00:59:27.550
You have to work.
你必须努力工作。

1072
00:59:28.030 --> 00:59:33.110
You can't just be, it's wonderful to be young and to be given an opportunity.
你不能仅仅是……年轻并获得机会固然很好。

1073
00:59:33.470 --> 00:59:38.650
And if you've got that spark, if you've got it and you can really sail out there, that's
如果你有那种天赋，如果你真的能驾驭它并闯出一片天地，那

1074
00:59:38.650 --> 00:59:39.030
great.
很棒。

1075
00:59:39.550 --> 00:59:41.830
And then I'd say, protect your heart.
然后我会说，保护好你的心。

1076
00:59:42.430 --> 00:59:47.550
Don't let your heart get hurt by strangers who say things about you or your work.
不要让你的心被那些对你或你的作品指手画脚的陌生人所伤害。

1077
00:59:47.690 --> 00:59:48.070
Yeah.
是的。

1078
00:59:48.250 --> 00:59:48.390
Yeah.
是的。

1079
00:59:48.570 --> 00:59:50.110
Because work is what got us here.
因为工作才是让我们走到今天的原因。

1080
00:59:50.250 --> 00:59:51.650
Work is what kind of keep us here.
工作也是让我们留在这里的原因。

1081
00:59:51.990 --> 00:59:56.530
I mean, it's like you guys were talking about the collaborative aspect of your work.
我的意思是，就像你们刚才谈到的工作中的协作层面一样。

1082
00:59:56.730 --> 00:59:58.610
And that was the focus of what you did.
那是你们所做工作的核心。

1083
00:59:58.750 --> 01:00:00.410
And that's what made it so wonderful.
也正是这一点让它变得如此美妙。

1084
01:00:01.210 --> 01:00:01.410
Yeah.
是的。

1085
01:00:01.710 --> 01:00:02.690
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

1086
01:00:02.690 --> 01:00:09.210
I feel like it's sometimes hard to be an artist because you do have to keep that open
我觉得作为一名艺术家有时很难，因为你必须保持那颗开放的

1087
01:00:09.210 --> 01:00:11.670
heart in order to do the work.
心才能完成工作。

1088
01:00:11.730 --> 01:00:17.510
But that makes it so that you're, I don't know, it's so easy to get wounded when you have
但这让你变得……我不知道，当你拥有那颗开放的心时，

1089
01:00:17.510 --> 01:00:18.350
that open heart.
太容易受伤了。

1090
01:00:18.810 --> 01:00:20.510
So it's such a balance.
所以这真是一种平衡。

1091
01:00:20.510 --> 01:00:21.650
It is.
确实如此。

1092
01:00:21.770 --> 01:00:23.210
It's a gift to be porous.
保持敏感是一种天赋。

1093
01:00:23.470 --> 01:00:27.230
It works great in your work, but it's not so great in the world outside.
它在你的工作中效果很好，但在外面的世界里却不那么好用。

1094
01:00:27.230 --> 01:00:28.570
It can be difficult.
这可能会很困难。

1095
01:00:28.930 --> 01:00:34.810
But I remember a producer, because I got very hurt one time in London by an awful interviewer,
但我记得有位制片人，因为有一次我在伦敦被一位糟糕的采访者伤害得很深，

1096
01:00:34.950 --> 01:00:36.590
and I literally left the tour.
我当时真的退出了巡回宣传。

1097
01:00:36.950 --> 01:00:40.630
And I remember the producer coming to me and saying, you're going to have to get a lot tougher.
我记得那位制片人来找我说，你必须变得更坚强一些。

1098
01:00:41.770 --> 01:00:43.270
You're going to have to toughen up.
你必须让自己硬起来。

1099
01:00:43.270 --> 01:00:44.890
But, you know, and he was right.
但是，你知道，他是对的。

1100
01:00:45.390 --> 01:00:50.070
Anyway, I appreciate being able to chat with you in a very open and safe way.
总之，我很感激能以一种非常开放和安全的方式与你交谈。

1101
01:00:50.230 --> 01:00:52.150
And I think we talked about some wonderful things.
我觉得我们聊了很多很棒的话题。

1102
01:00:52.310 --> 01:00:53.850
And I'm so happy for you.
我真为你感到高兴。

1103
01:00:54.290 --> 01:00:55.830
Oh, well, thank you.
哦，好的，谢谢你。

1104
01:00:56.090 --> 01:00:59.330
Happy for you, Jenna, that you're, that you've come through this.
珍娜，真为你感到高兴，你终于挺过来了。

1105
01:00:59.490 --> 01:01:03.610
Kathy, it was, it was such an honor to work with you.
凯西，能和你共事真是我的荣幸。

1106
01:01:03.770 --> 01:01:04.110
Yes.
是的。

1107
01:01:04.350 --> 01:01:09.610
You know, you did something at our first table read together that I never forgot.
你知道吗，我们在第一次围读剧本时，你做了一件事，我至今难忘。

1108
01:01:09.610 --> 01:01:16.350
You sat down at the table, and you had the script, and you got out a golden folding fan,
你坐在桌边，拿着剧本，然后掏出一把金色的折扇，

1109
01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:23.590
the kind that you go like, and you would fan yourself because you were hot, you know?
就是那种“唰”地一下打开，因为觉得热就扇风的那种，你记得吗？

1110
01:01:24.170 --> 01:01:33.630
And I thought to myself, one day, I am going to earn the right to fan myself with a golden fan.
当时我就想，总有一天，我也要赢得用金扇子扇风的资格。

1111
01:01:33.630 --> 01:01:38.310
And so, Kathy, my goal in life is to win a Tony.
所以，凯西，我的人生目标就是赢得托尼奖。

1112
01:01:39.730 --> 01:01:41.470
I want to do a Broadway show.
我想演一部百老汇剧目。

1113
01:01:41.590 --> 01:01:42.410
I want to win a Tony.
我想拿个托尼奖。

1114
01:01:42.590 --> 01:01:47.670
And when I walk up on that stage to accept my award, I am going to get out a golden fan,
等我走上领奖台发表获奖感言时，我会掏出一把金扇子，

1115
01:01:47.670 --> 01:01:50.830
and I am going to fan myself in your honor.
然后以你的名义扇扇风。

1116
01:01:51.850 --> 01:01:53.110
I'll wait for that.
我会等着那一天的。

1117
01:01:53.230 --> 01:01:54.090
I really will.
真的会等。

1118
01:01:54.390 --> 01:01:56.070
I'm excited for you to do that.
我很期待你做到那一点。

1119
01:01:57.390 --> 01:01:59.490
Angela, thank you so much.
安吉拉，太感谢你了。

1120
01:01:59.630 --> 01:02:01.470
It was great speaking with you today.
今天和你聊天很愉快。

1121
01:02:01.770 --> 01:02:02.970
I really appreciate it.
我真的很感激。

1122
01:02:03.630 --> 01:02:04.630
Thank you so much, Kathy.
非常感谢你，凯西。

1123
01:02:05.090 --> 01:02:07.310
You're a light in the world, and we just adore you.
你是这世上的一道光，我们都特别崇拜你。

1124
01:02:07.450 --> 01:02:08.370
So thank you so much.
真的非常感谢。

1125
01:02:08.510 --> 01:02:09.650
Thank you so much for the opportunity.
非常感谢你给我这个机会。

1126
01:02:10.330 --> 01:02:11.030
Bye, guys.
再见，伙计们。

1127
01:02:11.310 --> 01:02:11.530
Bye.
再见。

1128
01:02:11.650 --> 01:02:12.070
Take care.
保重。

1129
01:02:12.670 --> 01:02:12.950
Okay.
好的。

1130
01:02:16.770 --> 01:02:17.490
Oh, man.
天哪。

1131
01:02:17.490 --> 01:02:19.150
I just loved all of that.
我太喜欢刚才的一切了。

1132
01:02:19.350 --> 01:02:21.630
I loved just spending time with her.
我就是喜欢和她待在一起的感觉。

1133
01:02:21.730 --> 01:02:23.930
I really felt like we got to spend time with her.
我真的觉得我们和她共度了一段美好的时光。

1134
01:02:24.030 --> 01:02:24.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
01:02:24.510 --> 01:02:28.850
And I just love how happy she is in this new job, in this new chapter of her life.
我真的很喜欢她现在这份新工作，喜欢她人生新篇章中展现出的那种快乐。

1136
01:02:29.050 --> 01:02:30.690
You and I can really relate to that.
你和我对此真的深有同感。

1137
01:02:30.890 --> 01:02:31.050
Yeah.
没错。

1138
01:02:31.050 --> 01:02:35.690
And Matlock, you guys, airs on CBS every Thursday at 9 p.m.
各位，《马特洛克》每周四晚9点在CBS播出，

1139
01:02:36.050 --> 01:02:41.170
Eastern, and it's also streaming on Paramount Plus, and it's already been picked up for a second season.
东部时间，也可以在派拉蒙Plus上观看，而且已经续订了第二季。

1140
01:02:41.170 --> 01:02:47.670
Well, you know, Angela, we also said we would share a swipe up in our stories where people can learn more about lymphedema.
对了，安吉拉，我们之前也说过，会在快拍里分享一个链接，让大家了解更多关于淋巴水肿的信息。

1141
01:02:47.670 --> 01:02:52.870
And I would also like to include a link to the Breast Cancer Risk Assessment TeSt.
我还想附上一个乳腺癌风险评估测试的链接。

1142
01:02:53.130 --> 01:02:59.390
It is a test that you can take online at home to calculate your risk for developing breast cancer.
这是一个你可以在家在线完成的测试，用来计算你患乳腺癌的风险。

1143
01:02:59.550 --> 01:03:03.830
And it's kind of based on your age, breast density, family history.
它主要基于你的年龄、乳房密度和家族病史等因素。

1144
01:03:04.190 --> 01:03:12.430
And if you have an increased risk, you can share those results with your doctor, and you might qualify for additional diagnostic testing.
如果你发现风险增加，可以把结果告诉医生，或许你就有资格进行额外的诊断测试。

1145
01:03:12.430 --> 01:03:21.070
For example, if you are at a high risk, but you're younger than 40, you might qualify for an annual mammogram much sooner.
例如，如果你属于高风险人群，但年龄不到40岁，你可能就有资格提前进行年度乳房X光检查。

1146
01:03:21.630 --> 01:03:31.010
I have said before that my success with treatment is due to my very early detection, so it's really worth taking the teSt.
我之前说过，我治疗成功是因为发现得非常早，所以这个测试真的很值得一做。

1147
01:03:31.430 --> 01:03:32.450
Yeah, so important.
没错，非常重要。

1148
01:03:32.730 --> 01:03:34.910
Well, everyone, thanks for listening today.
好了，各位，感谢大家今天的收听。

1149
01:03:34.910 --> 01:03:40.490
We're going to be back with you on Friday with a special holiday bonus episode.
周五我们会带着一期特别的节日加更节目回来。

1150
01:03:40.810 --> 01:03:42.210
Yeah, we can't wait.
没错，我们已经迫不及待了。

1151
01:03:42.210 --> 01:03:43.190
It's really festive.
真的很有节日气氛。

1152
01:03:43.190 --> 01:03:44.090
It's really fun.
真的很有趣。

1153
01:03:44.250 --> 01:03:45.990
And we just hope you guys have a great week.
我们衷心希望大家能度过愉快的一周。

1154
01:03:46.150 --> 01:03:47.250
Know that we're thinking of you.
请记住，我们一直挂念着你们。

1155
01:03:47.390 --> 01:03:48.630
And we'll see you Friday.
我们周五见。

1156
01:03:48.890 --> 01:03:49.470
See you then.
到时候见。

1157
01:03:56.990 --> 01:03:59.090
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

